Z||000000||Seanh||07-16-2000||06:56 PM||||I had tons of trouble with my Factory Subwoofer and Amp system when I hooked up an aftermarket radio. I posted on here and got answers, now, Iv read tons of information on this system. If anyone is having trouble with their system, Feel Free to drop me a line at the address below. I can provide tons of help and informational sites. Thanks to all who have helped me. <P>Sean Heberly<BR>86 GT w/twin turbos<BR>sean@kdsi.net<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||07-16-2000||07:50 PM||||Twin Turbos?  Do tell us a little more about your combo, very interesting!<P>BTW, I'll probably be bugging you in the near future about the stock sub and aftermarket radio.<P><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||07-16-2000||09:21 PM||||For all those wondering about the twin turbos on my 86GT 2.8, I purchased the car with the turbos, but I recently had to replace one. So I cant take all the credit. Iv had the car on a Kansas track, It did the Quarter Mile in 12.6, thats with an automatic by the way. The car has 116,000 miles, so I am not really looking to red line it but I have had it up to 150 on the highway running at 3600 RPM's, so it wasnt working too hard.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BBBAD GT||07-17-2000||11:49 AM||||Is the V6 stock?  Thats great that you can get in the mid 12's with the twins, was it a custom fab job, or does somebody make a kit?  Got any pics/website?  What boost are you running?<P>I'm not sure if I believe 150 mph at only 3600 rpms.  I don't have the calculation in front of me, but if you were cruising at 60 mph in the same gear, then your rpms would be like 1000 or so.  Do you have a custom automatic?  Just curious.<P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Stock for now<BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT's Web Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula||07-17-2000||04:05 PM||||150 in 3rd gear wouldnt be the same 3 speed auto in my fiero LOL..... (mine gets about 125-130 at 5700 rpms)<P>150 would be something like 8000 rpms in the fiero 3 spd auto.  I guess you could have really weird gear ratios too to make it a 3 spd with a 12 sec qtr and 150+ mph top speed.<BR>But 3rd gear would slow you down horribly.<P>I would like to know more about your turbo setup, pics would be awesome!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||07-17-2000||04:06 PM||||Well, I might be wrong about the 150 mph @ 3600 rpms, I was over a year ago I tried it. They were on full boost, Im unsure what numbers that figured out to. And it was a custom job, but im sure if you were really interested you could find a kit for it somewhere out there. And, Yes, It is a custom automatic, 4 speed (with overdrive) in fact. I would like to talk more to the guy who owned it about everything, but hes in Jail at the time, and I dont think he knows anymore about it then I do. This was the same guy who had different ohm spark plug wires on each plug, and the spark plugs were held tight with masking tape. I dont know how he managed to put turbos on it?!? <P>Im working on Pictures, it might be a few more days though, Ill post them as soon as I get them back and scanned<P>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 07-17-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 07-17-2000).]||||reg||1
